// graphify MCP launcher snippet — merge into your project's `.mcp.json`
// under "mcpServers" (strip these `//` comments — JSON disallows them).
//
// Canonical launcher: the upstream `graphify-mcp` console script (shipped in
// graphifyy >= 0.8.36; MCP extra `graphifyy[mcp]`). Pin `graphifyy >= 0.8.42`.
//
// Prerequisites:
//   1. uv tool install graphifyy --with mcp     (see the two traps below)
//   2. graphify .                                (produces graphify-out/graph.json — the server reads it)
//
// TRAP 1 — do NOT launch via `uvx` / `uv tool run --from graphifyy`.
//   Both spin up an EPHEMERAL environment from the uv cache and never see the
//   `mcp` package baked into the installed tool-env, so the server dies with
//   `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mcp'`. Call the shim on PATH instead
//   (`~/.local/bin/graphify-mcp`), which is what the snippet below does.
//   Diagnosed 2026-08-27 on Inspector_bottles.
//
// TRAP 2 — there is NO `serve` subcommand.
//   `graphify-mcp serve <path>` exits 2 (argparse: unrecognized arguments).
//   The graph path is a positional argument: `graphify-mcp <path>`.
//
// TRAP 3 — `mcp` is NOT in graphifyy's dependencies (upstream bug), so it must
//   be baked in ONCE: `uv tool install graphifyy --with mcp --force`.
//   Do not pass `--with mcp` at runtime: it builds an overlay env and re-resolves
//   it on EVERY start, and the MCP connect handshake then misses its timeout.
//
// graphify MCP is OPTIONAL (enabled.yaml -> mcp-graphify.enabled: false). The
// `/graphify` skill stays the primary path; the MCP adds a live-query layer.
{
  "graphify": {
    "command": "graphify-mcp",
    "args": ["graphify-out/graph.json"]
  }
}
